      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based on your criteria, I'd rank the candidates as follows: \n\n1. Marcus Washington - His background as a high-energy leader with a direct communication style and rapid problem-solving skills suggests he'd thrive in the high-stakes boardroom environment. His experience managing large cross-functional teams also implies he's accustomed to navigating complex situations.\n\n2. James Sterling - As a former collegiate rowing captain, James has demonstrated leadership skills in a traditionally male-dominated environment. His experience in high-stakes restructuring projects also shows he can handle pressure. However, his background in traditional networking circles might make him less relatable to a diverse client base.\n\n3. Arjun Mehta - While Arjun has an impressive analytical track record, his background in community leadership and urban development initiatives might make him less familiar with the high-stakes, high-reward environment of Fortune 500 boards. His experience in boutique consulting also suggests he might not have the same level of exposure to large-scale, high-pressure projects.",
